course: dictionary
lesson: 10713
title: A formal word for a lie
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An untruth is a lie: a statement that is not true. It is a formal, polite word, so you will meet it in news, school and stories, where someone does not want to say «lie» bluntly. Plain words for it are lie and fib.
explain: «Some untruths are told out of love.» Here untruth means a lie, and the clue is told out of love: the person meant well. So an untruth is not always cruel.
explain: Untruth can also mean the state of not being true. Check which meaning fits by swapping in lie or fib. If the sentence still makes sense with a plain word, you have found the meaning.
fact: An untruth is a lie, a statement that is not true.
fact: «Untruth» is a formal word; «lie» and «fib» are plainer words for the same idea.
fact: A fib is an informal word for a small lie.
fact: A «white lie» is a small untruth told to protect someone's feelings, such as saying «I love it!» about a present you don't like.
fact: Spotting untruths online matters, because not everything you read is true.
exercise: «Some untruths are told out of love.» Which plain word could replace untruth here? | Song | Garden | Dance | *Lie
exercise: «A white lie is a small untruth told to protect someone's feelings.» What is a white lie? | *A small, kind untruth told to protect someone's feelings | A true story told very quietly | A word for a shade of paint | A big, cruel lie told to hurt someone
exercise: Ella says, «Untruths are formal, so I'd say fib instead.» Why is untruth called a formal word? | *It is a polite word for a lie, used in formal speech and writing | It means a happy song | It means the opposite of a lie, so it is always true | It only describes wet weather
test: «Politicians hide taxes and untruths the same way.» What does untruths mean here? | Happy songs | Sunny days | *Lies, statements that are not true | Pieces of cake
test: What kind of lie is a fib? | A question someone asks | A large, formal lie told in court | *A small, informal lie | A true statement
exam: Which sentence uses untruth as a formal word for a lie? | «The sun is a star.» | «The bus was late this morning.» | «Please pass the bread.» | *«Some untruths are told out of love.»
